    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "By severity and response, a second 5 g IV dose may be given (total 10 g), infused over 15 min (in extremis) to 2 h."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Most common:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " transient chromaturia (red urine), erythema, urine oxalate crystals, rash, increased BP, nausea, headache, infusion-site reactions."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Monitor BP during treatment (substantial rises can occur) and renal function for 7 days (acute renal failure with ATN and urine oxalate crystals reported)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Its deep red color interferes with colorimetric lab tests and can shut down hemodialysis machines (false blood-leak alarm). Chemically incompatible with sodium thiosulfate and sodium nitrite: don't give other cyanide antidotes in the same IV line."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
